hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2942","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abi Suraij al-Razi, that 'Amr ibn Mujammi' al-Kindi informed them, on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would visit the House (the Ka'bah)"","" circumambulate it seven times"","" pray two rak'ahs"","" and then it would become lawful for him to be intimate with women.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
